' Body of audio-timing.puml / audio-timing-dark.puml. No start marker, so
' PlantUML will not render this file directly, and naming one in a comment here
' breaks the include. See README.md.
'
' Stage order: services/voice/src/router.rs. What each stage costs and why the
' flat lanes are flat: ../SERVICES.md §4.
'
' Four documented timing constructs this build rejects, each found by bisecting
' against an error naming only a line number: `X has state, state`, a
' `0 <-> 10 : label` constraint, a `line:` suffix on a highlight colour, and a
' `:` inside a lane label. The packet markers and the highlight carry explicit
' fills because no skinparam reaches either; the waveform needs the style block
' in the wrapper for the same reason.

skinparam defaultFontName Inter
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam timingFontSize 12

title The 10 ms budget

header
<b>Widths are order, not measurement.</b>  Measured: the <b>10 ms period</b>, and <b>17.8 us</b> of control-plane overhead per message.
Lanes: a <b>speaker</b> at 50 packets/s, <b>voice</b> on its own UDP socket, <b>membership</b> from a session-view subscription, the <b>gateway</b>.
endheader

concise "**speaker**" as CL
robust "**voice**" as V
robust "**membership**" as S
robust "**gateway**" as G

@CL
0 is "frame n" $c_pkt
1 is {-}
10 is "frame n+1" $c_pkt
11 is {-}
20 is "frame n+2" $c_pkt

@V
0 is Idle
1 is Attribute
2 is Decrypt
3 is Decode
4 is Route
5 is Seal
8 is Send
9 is Idle
11 is Attribute
12 is Decrypt
13 is Decode
14 is Route
15 is Seal
18 is Send
19 is Idle

@S
0 is Warm
20 is Warm

@G
0 is "not on this path"
20 is "not on this path"

highlight 0 to 10 $c_frame : **one 10 ms frame**

caption \n**Route** reads a cached snapshot; a request here would put a round trip inside the budget.  **Seal** is N seals, one per listener, and that number sizes the pod.
